hey guys it's Jonah here so I recently  worked with Nestle bliss yoga drink as  the nutrition coach for their web  reality series to coach the contestants  on the importance of our digestive  system and also to put them through a  series of food-related challenges so if  you want to watch it the episodes be  sure to click on the link in my  description box I had a lot of fun on  set the production C was great the girls  were amazing and I got to speak in my  own native language here's a short clip  just to share with you well done ladies  well done for getting all this food on  the table Jerry and Avila Inga haha whoa  sumo mechana any add alarm' economy and  tinggi de la nutrition the topical  assist empanadas man and a terrible  goose button under tidak akan Department  a nutrition Makana le subpoena here our  digestive system is also known as the  second brain it is at the very center of  our core health so basically what I  shared in the clip is that optimal  digestion is key to a healthier and  fitter body optimal digestive function  means that our body is able to break  down food properly absorbing enough of  the right nutrients and eliminate the  waste that we don't need guys you could  be eating the cleanest most nutrient  rich diet in the world but if your body  isn't digesting properly you will not be  able to absorb all the good nutrients  from the food as a result waste  built up you retain water and your body  would turn excess calorie into fat some  of the most common digestive problems  are related to eating too much processed  food or junks high salt or sugar intake  not eating enough fiber fruits and  vegetables eating large portion in one  sitting and also poor eating habits such  as eating too quickly or skipping meals  so the basic questions to ask yourself  are do you always feel bloated or tired  at the end of a meal do you always feel  lack of energy do you struggle to lose  weight despite cutting back on excess  calories and doing regular exercise  so if you answer yes to two or three  questions it can mean that you might  have a sluggish digestion slow  metabolism and also issue with your  weight so I want to share with you  something that I've shared with the  contestants on the show which is five  foods to promote better digestion and as  a result you will increase in energy  feel less bloated you will start losing  weight more efficiently gain a flatter  tummy and also you will feel much better  from the inside and out the first group  is to eat food containing high  probiotics probiotics are often known as  the good bacteria because they keep your  gut healthy probiotics help move food  through your gut so food which are high  in probiotics include fermented foods  such as kimchi sauerkraut kombucha kefir  pickles miso  tempeh and of course yogurt yogurt is  one of the most widely available  probiotic containing foods but not all  yogurts are equally as beneficial so it  is very important to look for labels  that contain the live and active  cultures still the second group is to  consume food high in fiber I'm sure we  all know this and have been told too  many times to consume foods high in  fiber because it will not only help with  your digestion but it will keep you  fuller for much longer and also help  with weight loss  so this include pretty much all kinds of  vegetables all kinds of fruits grains  such as brown rice multigrain bread  whole wheat pasta barley your legumes  beans and all kinds of nuts and seeds if  however you do suffer from green or  bloating then avoid gas causing food  such as cabbage broccoli beans or  potatoes and the third group is to eat  food high in water water is extremely  important to the metabolic process and  helps move food through the digestive  tract so fiber can't function properly  without water if you consume a diet high  in fiber but lack in your fluid intake  you will still experience indigestion  gas and bloating besides drinking enough  water on a daily basis another great way  to increase your fluid intake is to eat  food high in water more than 90% such as  cucumbers zucchini leafy greens melons  citrus fruits berries tomatoes and  radishes these foods are also known as  high volume low calorie foods because  they can't keep you satisfied through a  low amount of calories so they are  excellent choices especially if your  goal is to cut back on excess calories  and still feel satisfied a lot of us  already know about the importance of  consuming food high in probiotics but we  tend to miss out on the importance of  food containing high prebiotics which  are equally just as important prebiotics  are non digestible or partially  digestible food ingredients that  stimulate the growth of healthy bacteria  in the colon so prebiotics act as food  for probiotics - simply put probiotics  eat prebiotics since fiber is the source  for prebiotics foods which are high in  fiber are typically high in prebiotics  some of the best examples include  asparagus bananas big roots leeks onions  garlic wheat bran artichokes chickpeas  and lentils and the final group you must  eat for a healthy digestion and also for  a flatter tummy is herbs and spices I  always tell my audience that herbs and  spices are the best way to season and  flavor your food without the additional  calories they are also known to  stimulate the production of digestive  enzyme for better food breakdown it can  also boost your metabolism help your  body to burn fat more quickly and also  relieve gas and bloating so some of my  favorites include ginger pepper mint  cinnamon turmeric cumin cayenne pepper  black pepper and cardamom you can add  them into your cooking or make team be  sure to watch my Asian detox tea video  to make them so the  secret to losing weight more efficiently  and to maintain a healthy weight long  term really comes down to your digestive  health if you have a better digestion  you will notice that you will have more  energy  no more bloating no more constipation no  more water retention and also a better  sense of overall well-being so if you  want to shut off the excess weight again  a flatter tummy and feel lighter  be sure to include these five food  groups into your diet if you find this  video to be helpful be sure to like it  and share it as well all the best  you  you
 

